WEBVTT

00:23:59.548 --> 00:24:01.545
It was exactly the same story.

00:24:01.569 --> 00:24:03.005
And that's not a genre, Chris.

00:24:03.029 --> 00:24:05.054
That's not like a vampire romance.

00:24:05.078 --> 00:24:07.538
That is so incredibly specific,

00:24:07.562 --> 00:24:10.726
and we were both -- I have chills
now talking about it.

00:24:10.750 --> 00:24:15.408
We sat there together and did the math
on when the idea had left me

00:24:15.432 --> 00:24:17.067
and when it had come to her,

00:24:17.091 --> 00:24:20.094
and we isolated it to
around the time that we met,

00:24:20.118 --> 00:24:23.989
and we like to think that it
actually was exchanged in the kiss,

00:24:24.013 --> 00:24:27.085
that the idea just jumped
from one novelist to another,

00:24:27.109 --> 00:24:30.323
and was like, "This novelist
is not going to be good enough for me.